<title>UK: BP says buys UK oil distributor Charringtons.</title>
<headline>BP says buys UK oil distributor Charringtons.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>BP Oil UK Ltd, a unit of British Petroleum Co Plc, said on Monday it had bought oil distributor Charrington Fuels Ltd for an unspecified amount.</p>
<p>BP said Charringtons would be operated by BP's commercial fuels business as a wholly-owned marketing subsidiary. BP called Charringtons Britain's largest independent oil distributor.</p>
<p>The company employs 430 people and has over 200 tankers delivering from 24 depots across Britain.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
